    "insert": "The exposé explores the potential of holographic AI assistants to enhance education by improving engagement, participation and accessibility. The study aims to address limitation of existing educational technologies such as VR and learning management systems by combining advanced holography with adaptive AI. The research uses a mixed-methods approach to evaluate the impact of holographic AI on learning process.\n re relevant to the problem statement and focus on important aspects like engagement, participation, and accessibility. The hook catches attention with it's statistics. The research questions are generally easy to understand for a broad audience. \n\nThe research questions should reflect clear and specific objectives, aligning with the purpose of the study.  However, one the research questions is hardly addressed in the exposé - \"In what ways can holographic AI provide personalised learning?\". This sub-question seems too broad. It is also not clarified why holographic AI is the optimal choice for an accessible educational technologies, which is stated one of the biggest shortcoming of VR apposed to the new technology.  To improve the exposé, refine the research questions to ensure they are more specific and are being addressed in the methodology.  Elaborate more on in what way the holographic assistance is more affordable or accessible than VR. Adding a definition of \"personalised learning\" within the theoretical framework could help provide clarity and context for the RQ.\n\nThe exposé has a good structure, it includes key elements such as the motivation, research questions, theoretical framhodology, some acknowledgement of limitations and a timeline. The example provided in the State of the Art section effectively demonstrates the potential of holography in education and aligns well with the problem space. \n\nIn the theoretical framework, it is important to explain key concepts and definitions from theory that are directly relevant to your topic. This includes describing the necessity of specific approaches or concepts and how they contribute to answering the RQs. The exposé introduces theories like Engagement Theory and TPACK. However, it is not clear they will be applied to address the practical challenges of integrating holographic AI into classrooms. The exposé doesn’t fully explain how these theories connect to the specific research questions or how they will guide data analysis. To improve this section, provide a detailed explanation of how each theory informs the study. Explain how these theories will guide the research design, data collection and analysis. As mentioned above, define the terminology of RQs for better clarity.\n\nThe mixed-methods approach is a good choice for studying both quantitative metrics (engagement, attention span) and qualitative insights (educator perspectives). The inclusion of diverse stakeholders gives a a comprehensive view of the technology’s potential. The exposé does a good job of addressing abstract criteria such as engagement by specifying how the collected data will be used to measure it. \n\nThe methodology should describe how you will answer all of the stated RQs, details of implementation - design and technical insights of the holographic AI assistant, what type of AI will power the technology and etc. The methodology should also specify the reasoning (why, what, and how) behind the choice of methods, that you will use in the research. \n\nThe current methodology lacks precision and clarity. It is unclear which holographic AI assistant will be evaluated—whether an existing open-source solution will be used or if the technology needs to be designed and implemented as part of the study. If an existing solution is to be used, it should have been explicitly mentioned and discussed in the State of the Art section. If the technology is yet to be developed, this aspect is entirely missing from the exposé. The technical details of the study are completely missing, leaving a gap in understanding the feasibility and implementation process. To further develop your methodological skills, you should focus more on the precise design of your AI-framework - state whether an existing holographic AI assistant will be used or if the technology will be developed. If it needs to be designed, include an outline of the design and technical specification.\n\nIn the evaluation part of methodology there is no explanation to why were 200 students and 50 teaching assistants chosen as sample sizes and wether they are representative of diverse demographics and educational settings.  The exposé briefly mentions ed-tech stakeholders and developers as contributors to evaluating scalability but does not provide further details. It is unclear how their opinions will be obtained, whether through interviews or other means.\nThere’s no discussion of how ethical considerations will be handled, such as privacy concerns or informed consent, especially given the use of minors as particiants. To improve this part, address ethical aspects thoroughly, including how informed consent will be obtained (especially for minors), and any potential risks associated with participation, wether the collected data represents different demograics and diversity. You might need to consult with the "
